hat's great about that is normally  that's sort of a shyster sign kind of  skeevy kind of oh no he's just taking  advantage of everybody character here  what's motivating him is true legitimate  love for his theatre for live  entertainment he wants this to work so  bad not because he's in debt but because  he loves it and that just sort of gives  you the idea that this this is not you  know a cynical movie and it takes the  more intelligent route in terms of its  premise again I don't want to oversell  this isn't this is not brilliant but  because these characters are so well  rounded and are so well developed and  the story the film never throws the  characters under the bus for the sake of  a goofy plot twist so it did at  some points give me the fields not again  not full-on not like up and not like  inside out but it gave me feels at a  couple points and they were legit they  just weren't as intensive as something  of say a higher caliber Disney or Pixar  or Miyazaki or what-have-you but for the  studio this is coming from I actually  might start looking forward to  illumination films from here on out I  mean this is really good it's really  solid I took my daughter she had a blast  I could tell all the kids in the theater  were loving it I actually really liked  that they used pop songs that was iffy  on that like because it never feels like  the film is just a showcase for the pop  songs because they go through so many  not only our character singing them but  they're using them you know to punctuate  moments as well and so they're not  except for the final sort of act when  the show gets put on these songs don't  get lingered on you know to be like ooh  and now here's this song like that  doesn't happen so much it just keeps  going and moving forward like he and  here's this song and it's on just long  enough for you to recognize it and get  the joke or get the moment or whatever  it is and then we move on to something  else it's fast paced but it's not  hyperactive it's not like this film  would have broken into my top 10 if I'd  caught it before the end of 2016 but  this is really good it's really solid  and 2016 was a pretty decent year for  animation overall and I'll include this  on that rationale so sing have you folks  seen it what did you think about it  whatever you thought drop something down  in the comments and let's talk about it  don't forget to like subscribe hit that  bell so you get notifications when I put  new stuff up you can follow me on  twitter at council of geeks check out  the council of geeks podcast available  on itunes and stitcher  and as for me I will be back as soon as  I can get my next fix  [Applause]
 

